_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":77.8,"pf":[],"description_full":"DICK'S Sporting Goods, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an omni-channel sporting goods retailer primarily in the United States. It provides hardlines, including sporting goods equipment, fitness equipment, golf equipment, and fishing gear products; and apparel. The company also offers footwear and accessories, such as athletic shoes for running, walking, tennis, fitness and cross training, basketball, and hiking; and specialty footwear comprising casual footwear and a complete line of cleats for team sports. In addition, it owns and operates Sporting Goods, Golf Galaxy, Public Lands, Moosejaw, and Going Going Gone! specialty concept stores; and DICK'S House of Sport and Golf Galaxy Performance Center, as well as GameChanger, a youth sports mobile app for live streaming, scheduling, communications, and scorekeeping. Further, the company owns and operates Foot Locker, which includes Foot Locker, Kids Foot Locker, Champs Sports, WSS and atmos banners. It offers its products online, as well as through its mobile apps. The company was formerly known as Dick'S Clothing and Sporting Goods, Inc. and changed its name to DICK'S Sporting Goods, Inc. in April 1999. DICK'S Sporting Goods, Inc. was incorporated in 1948 and is headquartered in Coraopolis, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lauren R. Hobart | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 31K people. Revenue per employee of $545K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $13K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Dick's Sporting Goods Inc is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $12.5B market cap on $17.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 97% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 87-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 31%.","The business throws off $400M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.81\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 17\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 6.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Shares offer a 20% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Insiders are net buyers (78% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","14 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can Dick's Sporting Goods (NYSE:DKS) Turn The Corner After A Tough Quarter?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/can-dicks-sporting-goods-nysedks-turn-the-corner-after-a-tough-quarter","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793916540.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Dick's Sporting Goods (DKS) Sees a More Significant Dip Than Broader Market: Some Facts to Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024963/dick-s-sporting-goods-dks-sees-a-more-significant-dip-than-broader-market-some-facts-to-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_6v2-3024963","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793916002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.272,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NIKE And 2 Other Elite Dividend Stocks 